1
00:00:01,471 --> 00:00:06,762
(Q31) In public discussion of business, we take certain values for granted.

2
00:00:06,762 --> 00:00:16,141
[对应小标题，  hard work = industriousness n. 勤勉] Today I'm going to talk about four of them: collaboration, hard work, creativity and excellence.

3
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:20,316
Most people would say they're all 'good things'.

4
00:00:20,316 --> 00:00:23,917
I'm going to suggest that's an over-simple view.

5
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:32,003
The trouble with these values is that they're theoretical concepts, removed from the reality of day-to-day business.

6
00:00:32,003 --> 00:00:43,512
[Q31答案句， value空前定位词原词， + 连接词 as a result, they can ... cause = result in ➡️ damage] Pursue values by all means, but be prepared for what may happen as a result.They can actually cause 【damage】, which is not at all the intention.

7
00:00:43,512 --> 00:00:47,720
(Q32) Business leaders generally try to do the right thing.

8
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:57,386
[Q32答案句， manage=deal with] But all too often the right thing backfires, if those leaders adopt values without understanding and managing the 【side effects】 that arise.

9
00:00:57,386 --> 00:01:02,121
The values can easily get in the way of what's actually intended.

10
00:01:02,121 --> 00:01:08,475
(Q33) [小标题定位] OK. So the first value I'm going to discuss is collaboration.

11
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:10,943
Er, let me give you an example.

12
00:01:10,943 --> 00:01:22,362
[Q33答案句： construct = build] On a management training course I once attended, we were put into groups and had to construct a bridge across a stream, using building blocks that we were given.

13
00:01:22,362 --> 00:01:29,976
(Q34) The rule was that everyone in the team had to move at least one building block during the construction.

14
00:01:29,976 --> 00:01:33,758
This was intended to encourage teamwork.

15
00:01:33,758 --> 00:01:37,681
But it was really a job best done by one person.

16
00:01:37,681 --> 00:01:46,496
[Q34答案句： descend into = experience] The other teams tried to collaborate on building the structure, and descended into confusion, with everyone getting in each other's way.

17
00:01:46,496 --> 00:01:50,426
(Q35) Our team leader solved the challenge brilliantly.

18
00:01:50,426 --> 00:02:02,596
She simply asked everyone in the team to move a piece a few centimetres, to comply with the rule, and then let the person in the team with an aptitude for puzzles like this build it alone.

19
00:02:02,596 --> 00:02:05,737
We finished before any other team.

20
00:02:05,737 --> 00:02:13,538
My point is that the task wasn't really suited to teamworking, so why make it one?

21
00:02:13,538 --> 00:02:31,961
[Q35答案句，跟疑似答案，] Teamwork can also lead to inconsistency - a common cause of poor sales.In the case of a smartphone that a certain company launched, one director wanted to target the business market, and another demanded it was aimed at consumers.

22
00:02:31,961 --> 00:02:41,792
(Q36) The company wanted both directors to be involved, so gave the product a consumer-friendly name, but marketed it to companies.

23
00:02:41,792 --> 00:02:46,189
The result was that it met the needs of neither group.

24
00:02:46,189 --> 00:02:52,963
It would have been better to let one director or the other have his way, not both.

25
00:02:52,963 --> 00:02:58,346
[Q36小标题] Now industriousness, or hard work.

26
00:02:58,346 --> 00:03:08,750
It's easy to mock people who say they work hard: after all, a hamster running around in a wheel is working hard - and getting nowhere.

27
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:20,304
[Q36答案句] Of course hard work is valuable, but only when properly targeted.&nbsp;&nbsp;Otherwise it wastes the 【resources】that companies value most - time and energy.&nbsp;

28
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:22,860
And that's bad for the organisation.

29
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:32,982
(Q37) There's a management model that groups people according to four criteria: clever, hard-working, stupid and lazy.

30
00:03:32,982 --> 00:03:39,818
[Q37答案句] Here 'lazy' means having a rational determination not to carry out unnecessary tasks.

31
00:03:39,818 --> 00:03:43,467
It doesn't mean trying to avoid work altogether.

32
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:58,635
(Q38) Most people display two of these characteristics, and the most valuable people are those who are both clever and lazy: they possess intellectual clarity, and they don't rush into making decisions.

33
00:03:58,635 --> 00:04:05,705
They come up with solutions to save the time and energy spent by the stupid and hard-working group.

34
00:04:05,705 --> 00:04:13,791
Instead of throwing more man-hours at a problem, the clever and lazy group looks for a more effective solution.

35
00:04:13,791 --> 00:04:17,664
[Q38跟定位，小标题] Next we come to creativity.

36
00:04:17,664 --> 00:04:26,394
This often works well - creating an attention-grabbing TV commercial, for example, might lead to increased sales.

37
00:04:26,394 --> 00:04:30,115
But it isn't always a good thing.

38
00:04:30,115 --> 00:04:37,335
[Q38答案句] Some advertising campaigns are remembered for their creativity, without having any effect on sales. This happened a few years ago with the launch of a 【chocolate bar】:&nbsp;

39
00:04:37,335 --> 00:04:49,255
(Q39) subsequent research showed that plenty of consumers remembered the adverts, but had no idea what was being advertised.

40
00:04:49,255 --> 00:04:59,491
The trouble is that the creator derives pleasure from coming up with the idea, and wrongly assumes the audience for the campaign will share that feeling.

41
00:04:59,491 --> 00:05:12,454
A company that brings out thousands of new products may seem more creative than a company that only has a few, but it may be too creative, and make smaller profits.

42
00:05:12,454 --> 00:05:19,373
[Q39答案句， target = particular， as a response to = to solve] Creativity needs to be targeted, to solve a problem that the company has identified.

43
00:05:19,373 --> 00:05:24,532
[Q39干扰项， 以为novel = particular， 所以就写成了product] Just coming up with more and more novel products isn't necessarily a good thing.

44
00:05:24,532 --> 00:05:27,853
(Q40) And finally, excellence.

45
00:05:27,853 --> 00:05:36,307
We all know companies that claim they 'strive for excellence', but it takes a long time to achieve excellence.

46
00:05:36,307 --> 00:05:43,055
In business, being first with a product is more profitable than having the best product.

47
00:05:43,055 --> 00:05:58,562
[Q40跟定位 pioneer] A major study of company performance compared pioneers - that is, companies bringing out the first version of a particular product – with followers, the companies that copied and improved on that product.

48
00:05:58,562 --> 00:06:14,227
[Q40答案句] The study found that the pioneers commanded an average 【market share】 of 29 percent, while the followers achieved less than half that, only 13 percent - even though their product might have been better.

49
00:06:14,227 --> 00:06:24,297
Insisting on excellence in everything we do is time-consuming, wastes energy and leads to losing out on opportunities.

50
00:06:24,297 --> 00:06:29,834
Sometimes, second-rate work is more worthwhile than excellence.

51
00:06:29,834 --> 00:06:32,334
'Make sure it's excellent' sounds like a good approach to business, but the 'just-get-started' approach is likely to be more successful. “

